  "rootCause": "computeHoldReasons always emitted ActiveRun whenever activeRun != Nothing, conflating 'run event not yet closed' with 'completion must remain held'. After the production C9 submit, the BCB barrier has already cleared; the residual activeRun is bookkeeping for a run whose AgentTurnDone (C8) has not yet been delivered but whose semantic completion has been declared (C10).",
  "originalRepair": "ActiveRun is suppressed from the hold set ONLY in handleTaskCompletionCommitted when model.submitCount >= 1.",
  "originalRepairFailure": "submitCount is a monotonic task-level counter. The R11 adversarial sequence (R1 submit+close, R2 run, TaskCompletionCommitted C2) demonstrated that a stale R1 submit authorizes R2's commit, because submitCount=1 from R1 persists into the R2 phase.",
  "refinedRepair": "ActiveRun is suppressed from the hold set ONLY in handleTaskCompletionCommitted when model.commitReadyRun == model.activeRun. commitReadyRun is a Maybe RunRef bound at SubmitAndExitSeen to the activeRun at that instant, and invalidated on every event that transitions activeRun (RunStarted, AgentTurnDone, ExecuteTurnPreludeEnter, ContinuationStarted).",
  "r11AdversarialSequence": {
    "chronology": [
      "TaskStarted T",
      "RunStarted R1",
      "SubmitAndExitSeen S1",
      "AgentTurnDone R1",
      "RunStarted R2",
      "TaskCompletionCommitted C2"
    ],
    "expected": "TaskCompletionCommittedWhileHeld ActiveRun",
    "preRefinement": "got Nothing (PASS for original R11-test logic, but this meant the model incorrectly accepted C2 because submitCount=1 from R1 satisfied the suppression)",
    "postRefinement": "got Just (TaskCompletionCommittedWhileHeld ActiveRun) \u2014 commitReadyRun was invalidated by RunStarted R2 and AgentTurnDone R1, so the suppression no longer applies"
  },
